The portable C as a program of 32 bits in the scenario command: what it is
expected to show otherwise than the original. A patch of
harness/goldens/command.txt, see harness/goldens.py: a line with - is the
golden's, a line with + is what is expected in its place.
Deviation: 1 of src/portable_c/DEVIATIONS.md
Why: a command of the program of 32 bits finds no memory above the megabyte,
since the extender holds all of it while the program is in the memory, and
answers for the BIOS: `mem` is told that there is none, and goes by the two
bytes of the clock's memory then, which have 128K more than the BIOS tells a
command of the original. So much more are the extended memory in all, what is
used of it, and the total memory. The program of 16 bits has no patch here

